# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# Scrambling 2NT (`competitive.scrambling_2nt.play`; convention-card
# competitive_bidding/scrambling_2nt; Robert S. Todd, Advancing in
# Bridge 555; PBS btn/Scrambling_2NT.btn): when advancer must bid
# after partner's takeout double of their raise, (1M) P (2M) X (P) 2NT
# is not natural: it shows two places to play, both minors, and asks
# the doubler to bid his lower four-card suit; advancer passes or
# corrects. A free 2NT (RHO has bid) would be good/bad, not written.
#
# Here: four or more in each minor, no five-card suit and no four-card
# unbid major (that is bid instead), 0-10 HCP (with more, game or a
# jump). Notes: scrambling-2nt.notes.md.

module scrambling-2nt "Scrambling 2NT"
  needs  base
  needs  takeout-double
  skill  competitive_bidding/scrambling_2nt
  card   competitive.scrambling_2nt.play

after (1M) P (2M) X (P) | (1M) P (2M) P (P) X (P)
  2N  "Scrambling: both minors, pick one"
      alert  artificial
      shows C>=4, D>=4, C<=5, D<=5, C+D>=8, hcp<=10, S<=3 | M is S, H<=3 | M is H
      sets  ask=scramble
      priority 1

# The doubler: his lower four-card minor.
when asked scramble
  3C  "Four or more clubs"                         shows C>=4
      priority 1
  3D  "Diamonds: fewer than four clubs"            shows D>=4
after (1M) P (2M) X (P) 2N (P) 3C (P) | (1M) P (2M) P (P) X (P) 2N (P) 3C (P)
  P   "Clubs will do"                              shows C>=D
      priority 1
  3D  "Diamonds: longer"                           shows D>C
      priority 1
